# Pin the registry for everyone, on every machine.
#
# The VPS resolves npm through a Tencent Cloud mirror by default, so an
# `npm install` run there rewrites every `resolved` URL in package-lock.json
# to mirrors.tencentyun.com — a host that only exists inside that network.
# The lockfile then travels through git, and the next install anywhere else
# dies with ENOTFOUND on all 500+ tarballs (npm reports this as the rather
# unhelpful "Exit handler never called").
#
# This has now bitten us twice: fixed in 8f5b3e6, reintroduced by the
# reminders/mail work. Pinning it here fixes the cause rather than the
# symptom, because a project .npmrc overrides the machine-level config.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
